# gatewayApiCall reach (to decide the scope of the header):
$ grep -rln "gatewayApiCall" services/gateway/src        # 31 files, ~250 call sites (ORB voice tools + gemini-operator)
$ grep -rn "requireServiceOrAdmin" services/gateway/src/routes   # approvals, cicd, delivery, governance-controls, self-healing (/report), specs, plans-spar, ...
# e.g. services/gateway/src/services/orb-tools/self-healing-tools.ts:63 POST /api/v1/self-healing/report sends no header today (route is
# requireServiceOrAdmin, self-healing.ts:402); adding the service token to EVERY gatewayApiCall would silently give that call, and any other
# header-less call to a requireServiceOrAdmin route, service authority. So the header is added only for /api/v1/worker/* paths (normalised
# pathname), and a caller-supplied Authorization still wins.
# Host: gatewayBaseUrl() = process.env.GATEWAY_URL || http://localhost:${PORT||8080} (developer-tools.ts:101-103). Staging container env sets
# GATEWAY_URL=https://preview-aws-gateway.vitanaland.com (.github/workflows/AWS-STAGE-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml:1251), the gateway's own URL.
# The token is not sent to a non-gateway host.

